# The claude.ai cloud environment's "Environment variables" field, as code
# (HIMMEL-5163). The platform has no API or repo file that creates an
# environment (docs/setup/cloud-environment.md#why-this-is-a-paste-not-a-command),
# so this file is the one source the paste block and the self-check both read:
#   bash scripts/cloud/check-env.sh --print   # the dialog's fields, from this file
#   bash scripts/cloud/check-env.sh           # a session compares itself to it
# One KEY=VALUE per line; never put a secret here (every user of the
# environment can read these values). `# rev: N` is the setup-script revision
# the paste block prints: bump it to force the platform's cached snapshot to
# rebuild.
# rev: 5
JIRA_PROJECT_KEY=HIMMEL
BASH_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS=600000
BASH_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS=600000
